  "details": "some instances of thumbnails are cropped and some aren't, some are even zoomed in (ie: Beta Portal)\n\nalso, it looks like all recent thumbnails have started being downsampled to 800x600, which contradicts the stated 1200x900 ideal resolution.\n\nI think some clearer guides and templates should be in order.\n\nI think safe zones should be overlaid on the in-editor thumbnail capture\n\nI think the SDK control panel tooltips should be updated to reflect the 800x600 resolution change\n\nI think the way thumbnails should be displayed should be more consistent. It's currently really hard to put words on a thumbnail and it not be cut off somewhere (ie: Beta Portal)\n\nImage Gallery\n\nImage 1: VRChat SDK showing \"Image Size 1200x900\"\n\nImage 2: my browser showing the image is actually 800x600\n\nImage 3: a typical world portal with the default appearance\n\nImage 4: the same world portal with the Beta design. note how the thumbnail is cut off even more than usual, and is stretched horizontally a whole lot.",
